==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|thereat}}, {{m|enm|ther-at}}, {{m|enm|þeratte}}, {{m|enm|þerat}}, from {{inh|en|ang|þǣræt}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*þārat}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*þarat}}, equivalent to {{com|en|there|at}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ðɛːɹˈæt/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-thereat.wav|Audio (Southern England)}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv|-}}

# There; at that [[place]].
